From 3ab69fab0a4f6fecccfa8f4971e512dbee2f533b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 07:29:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Move the privileged backend from Apps Script to a Supabase
 Edge Function
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Azerconnect's corporate proxy blocks the `google-app-script-base`
application, so script.google.com was unreachable for every user on the
network. That broke sign-in itself, not just the Admin Panel: role
resolution ran through the Apps Script Web App, so loginWithPassword()
failed with "Unable to reach the authorization service" after Supabase had
already verified the password. No deployment setting could fix it — the
block is at the network, ahead of the request.

The new admin-api Edge Function answers on the same *.supabase.co origin
the app already uses for Supabase Auth, which the network demonstrably
permits (password verification was working throughout).

The port is faithful — same action names, request/response shapes, and
server-side checks (verify the access token against Supabase itself, then
re-check admin_permissions for every admin action; never trust a role or
isAdmin flag from the client). Three things changed deliberately:

- resolveRole moved from GET with the token in the query string to POST
  with it in the body. The query-string form existed only because Apps
  Script Web Apps cannot answer a CORS preflight; Edge Functions can.
- bootstrapAdmin's "already used" guard now asks whether any
  admin_permissions row exists, rather than reading a script property that
  has no per-function equivalent. That is the condition it actually
  protects, and it needs no stored state.
- debugResolve was not ported. It was a temporary diagnostic that its own
  comment said to remove once bootstrap was confirmed working.

js/google.js becomes js/backend.js with its public API unchanged, so
auth.js, app.js and the Admin Panel modules are untouched apart from stale
references in their doc comments. apps-script/Code.gs is deleted rather
than left behind, following how this repo retired the dev-mode auth
provider: one source of truth, with the history in git.

Deploy steps, the reasoning behind --no-verify-jwt, and a one-command
verification are in supabase/functions/admin-api/README.md. Nothing needs
configuring: Supabase injects SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
into the function environment, so the service_role key stays out of this
repository.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
